    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The crusaders had too few men to surround the city, and a first assault on 13 June failed for lack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-engine">siege engines</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timber</a> and materials from ships that reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a> let the crusaders build two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-tower">siege towers</a>, a ram and ladders in almost three weeks, and the city was entered on 15 July.</li><li>Modern estimates put the dead of the siege and massacre at between 3,000 and 10,000, far below the 70,000 or 100,000 given by some contemporary Arab sources.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The city's water came from deep cisterns, while the crusaders had only the spring of En-Gihon, whose flow dropped considerably in summer; most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> and cisterns near the city had been made unusable.</p></aside>
    </section>

